{{if .ReferenceDriven}}### Visual fidelity contract

- UI mockups and design images are required visual targets, not loose styling
  inspiration. Match their composition, hierarchy, spacing, controls, borders,
  typography roles, color roles, and state presentation as closely as Omarchy's
  supported APIs allow.
- Supplied logos, app icons, and brand images must be used in the corresponding
  visible locations. Raster assets do not need to be recreated as vectors.
- The implementation may adapt dimensions for bar orientation, available
  screen space, accessibility, and theme tokens, but it must document every
  material deviation and obtain the user's approval rather than silently
  substituting generic generated UI.
- Static validation and a successful runtime load do not prove visual fidelity;
  acceptance requires human comparison of the plugin-only screenshot with the
  confirmed design references.
